  "meta": {
    "space": "embeddings_ability.npy",
    "projection": "classical MDS + SMACOF, canonically oriented",
    "clustering": "average-linkage agglomerative on cosine distance, 2 levels",
    "cards": 97,
    "unresolved": [],
    "note": "Positions are LOCAL to this deck and are not atlas positions — the deck is re-laid-out from its own cards, which is the whole point. Anything that draws this must say so.",
    "named_by": "deck-cartographer",
    "cartographer_notes": [
      "city-1 is 34 of 97 cards, but the mass that does work is city-2 (28): the token makers, converters, refills and pumps all sit in one place, which is what a linear critical-mass deck looks like from above.",
      "city-4 carries verified_count 5 of 8 — the densest verified block on the map. The drain is the engine on the record, not a theory; city-2's 5 verified sit across 28 cards.",
      "Deflecting Swat is the map's odd member. It clusters into city-2-hood-0 among the token payoffs, but it is a free instant you hold up, and every other card that does that job is in city-6. I read this as a placement artifact, not a discovery — membership left untouched.",
      "Olivia's Wrath is loose in the same neighbourhood for the same kind of reason: it is the one card in city-2 that removes bodies rather than adding or counting them. Worth knowing it lives inside the width engine, since five of the deck's creatures are not Vampires and the wrath hits them.",
      "Vampire Socialite sits in city-2-hood-1 with two cost reducers and a one-drop; it is a +1/+1 counter payoff and reads closer to city-0's crew. The hood's other three do share the 'make the second cast happen' job, so the name holds for the majority.",
      "city-3, city-4, city-5 and city-6 each contain exactly one neighbourhood identical to the city. There is no split to name, so those four hood ids are omitted deliberately rather than given a synonym of their parent.",
      "city-1-hood-3 is the cleanest split on the map: the two basics and the two lands that check for a basic type. That is a real dependency, not a leftover bucket."
    ]
  },
